7592186045585 true] [17592186396072 1071 "Find the radius and center of the circle whose equation is\n$2{x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}-8x+8y+3=0.$" 13194139533467 17592186045585 true] [17592186396072 1072 #uuid "0485f61e-5d32-5461-91b2-4119de37bba9" 13194139533467 17592186045585 true] [17592186396072 1074 "To find the center and radius of the circle, we need to group $x$ and $y$ terms and complete the squares.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}-8x+8y+3 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-4x+4y & =-\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ ({x}^{2}-4x)+({y}^{2}+4y) & =-\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ ({x}^{2}-2\\cdot 2x+{2}^{2})+({y}^{2}+2\\cdot 2y+{2}^{2}) & =-\\frac{3}{2}+{2}^{2}+{2}^{2} \\\\ ({x}^{2}-2\\cdot 2x+4)+({y}^{2}+2\\cdot 2x+4) & =\\frac{13}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can factor the perfect square and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-2)^{2}+{(y+2)}^{2} & =\\frac{13}{2} \\\\ (x-2)^{2}+{(y-(-2))}^{2} & ={(\\sqrt{\\frac{13}{2}})}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the circle is centered at $(2,-2)$ and its radius is $\\sqrt{\\frac{13}{2}}.$" 13194139533467 17592186045585 true] [17592186396073 1075 #edb/ref 17592186396074 13194139533467 17592186045585 true] [17592186396073 1075 #edb/ref 17592186396075 13194139533467 17592186045585 true] [17592186396073 1075 #edb/ref 17592186396076 13194139533467 17592186045585 true] [17592186396073 1075 #edb/ref 17592186396077 13194139533467 17592186045585 true] [17592186396073 1075 #edb/ref 17592186396078 13194139533467 17592186045585 true] [17592186396073 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533467 17592186045585 true] [17592186396073 1077 "selection" 13194139533467 17592186045585 true] [17592186396073 1079 #edb/ref 17592186396078 13194139533467 17592186045585 true] [17592186396073 1080 #uuid "8bd2771d-4f88-578f-9fd3-675729a93312" 13194139533467 17592186045585 true] [17592186396074 1081 "center: $(-2,-2)$, radius: $\\sqrt{\\frac{13}{2}}$" 13194139533467 17592186045585 true] [17592186396074 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533467 17592186045585 true] [17592186396074 1084 