 "q-6913" 13194139533467 17592186045585 true] [17592186396113 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533467 17592186045585 true] [17592186396113 1071 "Find all of the vertical asymptotes of the function $f(x)=\\frac{x}{{x}^{3}+2x}.$" 13194139533467 17592186045585 true] [17592186396113 1072 #uuid "2d87d550-5004-5d22-b9a3-b2335e96082d" 13194139533467 17592186045585 true] [17592186396113 1074 "To find the vertical asymptotes of a rational function, we factor the numerator and denominator and cancel any common factors. Then, we set the denominator equal to zero and solve for $x.$\n\nFactoring the numerator and denominator and canceling any common factors, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\frac{x}{{x}^{3}+2x} \\\\  & =\\frac{x}{x({x}^{2}+2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{x}}{\\cancel{x}({x}^{2}+2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we set the denominator equal to zero:\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+2=0\n$$\n\nThis equation does not have any real solutions. Therefore, $f(x)$ does not have any vertical asymptotes." 13194139533467 17592186045585 true] [17592186396114 1075 #edb/ref 17592186396115 13194139533467 17592186045585 true] [17592186396114 1075 #edb/ref 17592186396116 13194139533467 17592186045585 true] [17592186396114 1075 #edb/ref 17592186396117 13194139533467 17592186045585 true] [17592186396114 1075 #edb/ref 17592186396118 13194139533467 17592186045585 true] [17592186396114 1075 #edb/ref 17592186396119 13194139533467 17592186045585 true] [17592186396114 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533467 17592186045585 true] [17592186396114 1077 "selection" 13194139533467 17592186045585 true] [17592186396114 1079 #edb/ref 17592186396119 13194139533467 17592186045585 true] [17592186396114 1080 #uuid "cdc4a2be-1828-5c44-9645-c520108c6c2f" 13194139533467 17592186045585 true] [17592186396115 1081 "x=-2,\\,x=0,\\,x=2" 13194139533467 17592186045585 true] [17592186396115 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533467 17592186045585 true] [17592186396115 1084 #uuid "b2a272db