,$ the length of the horizontal radius must be $a=\\sqrt{9}=3.$\n\n- Since ${b}^{2}=18,$ the length of the vertical radius must be $b=\\sqrt{18}=3\\sqrt{2}.$\n\nSo the semi-major axis has length $b=3\\sqrt{2},$ and the semi-minor axis has length $a=3.$\n\nTherefore, the major axis has length $2b=2\\cdot 3\\sqrt{2}=6\\sqrt{2},$ and the minor axis has length $2a=2\\cdot 3=6.$" 13194139533467 17592186045585 true] [17592186396127 1075 #edb/ref 17592186396128 13194139533467 17592186045585 true] [17592186396127 1075 #edb/ref 17592186396129 13194139533467 17592186045585 true] [17592186396127 1075 #edb/ref 17592186396130 13194139533467 17592186045585 true] [17592186396127 1075 #edb/ref 17592186396131 13194139533467 17592186045585 true] [17592186396127 1075 #edb/ref 17592186396132 13194139533467 17592186045585 true] [17592186396127 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533467 17592186045585 true] [17592186396127 1077 "selection" 13194139533467 17592186045585 true] [17592186396127 1079 #edb/ref 17592186396132 13194139533467 17592186045585 true] [17592186396127 1080 #uuid "bef4ba21-7e9c-5949-8c09-0a45d37f8298" 13194139533467 17592186045585 true] [17592186396128 1081 "$6\\sqrt{2}$ and $3$" 13194139533467 17592186045585 true] [17592186396128 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533467 17592186045585 true] [17592186396128 1084 #uuid "d2368068-c473-5919-aff6-53a14b246b5c" 13194139533467 17592186045585 true] [17592186396129 1081 "$3\\sqrt{2}$ and $3$" 13194139533467 17592186045585 true] [17592186396129 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533467 17592186045585 true] [17592186396129 1084 #uuid "801b88de-1112-5c33-bd1b-ddb864de2c6f" 13194139533467 17592186045585 true] [17592186396130 1081 "$6$ and $3$" 13194139533467 17592186045585 true] [17592186396130 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533467 17592186045585 true] [17592186396130 1084 #uuid "dcd49079-798b-58f7-8490-cd6fb613a033" 13194139533467 17592186045585 true] [17592186396131 1081 "$18$ and $9$" 13194139533467 17592186045585 true] [17592186396131 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533467 17592186045585 true] [17592186396131 1084 #uuid "d5b72ba2-9df1-5acc-b385-173c4e36f9a6" 13194139533467 17592186045585 true] [17592186396132 1081 "$6\\sqrt{2}$ and $6$" 13194139533467 17592186045585 true] [17592186396132 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533467 17592186045585 true] [17592186396132 1084 #uuid "7c6ef04e-258f-5d68-a139-8ed8a39c2ddc" 13194139533467 17592186045585 true] [17592186396133 1068 #edb/ref 17592186396134 13194139533467 17592186045585 true] [17592186396133 1069 "q-7597" 13194139533467 17592186045585 true] [17592186396133 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533467 17592186045585 true] [17592186396133 1071 "What are the lengths of the major and minor axes of an ellipse with equation \n$\\frac{{x}^{2}}{20}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{16}=1?$" 13194139533467 17592186045585 true] [17592186396133 1072 #uuid "e572cb8d-0721-59ec-897a-5e0fa685feb4" 13194139533467 17592186045585 true] [17592186396133 1074 "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn the given equation, we have ${a}^{2}=20$ and ${b}^{2}=16.$\n\n- Since ${a}^{2}=20,$ the length of the horizontal radius must be $a=\\sqrt{20}=2\\sqrt{5}.$\n\n- Since ${b}^{2}=16,$ the length of the vertical radius must be $b=\\sqrt{16}=4.$\n\nSo the semi-major axis has length $a=2\\sqrt{5},$ and the semi-minor axis has length $b=4.$\n\nTherefore, the major axis has length $2a=2\\cdot 2\\sqrt{5}=4\\sqrt{5},$ and the minor axis has length $2b=2\\cdot 4=8.$" 13194139533467 17592186045585 true] [17592186396134 1075 #edb/ref 17592186396135 13194139533467 17592186045585 true] [17592186396134 1075 #edb/ref 17592186396136 13194139533467 17592186045585 true] [17592186396134 1075 #edb/ref 17592186396137 13194139533467 17592186045585 true] [17592186396134 1075 #edb/ref 17592186396138 13194