\\,Q=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,R=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 & 3 \\\\ 3 & -4 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139533467 17592186045585 true] [17592186396175 1072 #uuid "17761662-c8e1-5053-be1d-f17ca1632a52" 13194139533467 17592186045585 true] [17592186396175 1074 "- For the matrix $P$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(P)=4\\cdot 6-8\\cdot 3=0.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(P)=0,$ we conclude that $P$ is not invertible. Since $P$ is a square matrix that is not invertible, we also say that $P$ is singular.\n\n- For the matrix $Q$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(Q)=1\\cdot 1-(-1)\\cdot (-1)=0.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(Q)=0,$ we conclude that $Q$ is not invertible. Since $Q$ is a square matrix that is not invertible, we also say that $Q$ is singular.\n\n- The matrix $R$ is a $2\\times 3$ matrix. So, it is not invertible. Since the matrix is not square, we can't say that it's singular.\n\nTherefore, only $P$ and $Q$ are singular." 13194139533467 17592186045585 true] [17592186396176 1075 #edb/ref 17592186396177 13194139533467 17592186045585 true] [17592186396176 1075 #edb/ref 17592186396178 13194139533467 17592186045585 true] [17592186396176 1075 #edb/ref 17592186396179 13194139533467 17592186045585 true] [17592186396176 1075 #edb/ref 17592186396180 13194139533467 17592186045585 true] [17592186396176 1075 #edb/ref 17592186396181 13194139533467 17592186045585 true] [17592186396176 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533467 17592186045585 true] [17592186396176 1077 "selection" 13194139533467 17592186045585 true] [17592186396176 1079 #edb/ref 17592186396181 13194139533467 17592186045585 true] [17592186396176 1080 #uuid "aa5359f3-29e9-58eb-b41e-ef40c0bf51eb" 13194139533467 17592186045585 true] [17592186396177 1081 "$P$ and $R$ only" 13194139533467 17592186045585 true] [17592186396177 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533467 17592186045585 true] [17592186396177 1084 #uuid "bdb0a517-2a62-5ad4-abb7-32db925dcbb8" 13194139533467 17592186045585 true] [17592186396178 1081 "$Q$ and $R$ only" 13194139533467 17592186045585 true] [17592186396178 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533467 17592186045585 true] [17592186396178 1084 #uuid "378c3d9c-f434-5a36-b4c6-e35a124290f2" 13194139533467 17592186045585 true] [17592186396179 1081 "$Q$ only" 13194139533467 17592186045585 true] [17592186396179 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533467 17592186045585 true] [17592186396179 1084 #uuid "4ccb69d4-cf84-531e-a891-dec63188d912" 13194139533467 17592186045585 true] [17592186396180 1081 "$P$ only" 13194139533467 17592186045585 true] [17592186396180 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533467 17592186045585 true] [17592186396180 1084 #uuid "e1648b74-cbef-5884-9e5c-c49ee87da068" 13194139533467 17592186045585 true] [17592186396181 1081 "$P$ and $Q$ only" 13194139533467 17592186045585 true] [17592186396181 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533467 17592186045585 true] [17592186396181 1084 #uuid "94c1155a-b3ff-59dd-b24f-e9f04aac265d" 13194139533467 17592186045585 true] [17592186396182 1068 #edb/ref 17592186396183 13194139533467 17592186045585 true] [17592186396182 1069 "q-8049" 13194139533467 17592186045585 true] [17592186396182 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533467 17592186045585 true] [17592186396182 1071 "Let \n$T:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ x\\end{aligned}].$\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $T(kv)=kT(v)$ for any real $2\\times 1$ column vector $v$ and real scalar $k$\nII. $T({v}_{1}+{v}_{2})=T({v}_{1})+T({v}_{2})$ for any real $2\\times 1$ column vectors ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}$\nIII. $T$ is **NOT** a linear transformation" 13194139533467 17592186045585 true] [17592186396182 1072 #uuid "72a3fd90-5133-5a81-a0e8-33ac74b2d520" 13194139533467 17592186045585 true] [17592186396182 1074 "A linear transformation $T$ satisfies two properties:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & T[\\begin{aligned}kx \\\\ ky\\end{aligned}]=kT[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}], \\\\  & T[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{1}+{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=T[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{1}\\end{aligned}]+T[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Checking the first condition, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T[\\begin{aligned}kx \\\\ ky\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ kx\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & \\ne kT[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}].\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{T}$ is not a linear transformation.\n\n- Checking the second condition, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{1}+{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ {x}_{1}+{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ {x}_{1}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & \\ne T[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{1}\\end{aligned}]+T[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}].\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, only statement III is true." 13194139533467 17592186045585 true] [17592186396183 1075 #edb/ref 17592186396184 13194139533467 17592186045585 true] [17592186396183 1075 #edb/ref 17592186396185 13194139533467 17592186045585 true] [17592186396183 1075 #edb/ref 17592186396186 13194139533467 17592186045585 true] [17592186396183 1075 #edb/ref 17592186396187 13194139533467 17592186045585 true] [17592186396183 1075 #edb/ref 17592186396188 13194139533467 17592186045585 true] [17592186396183 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533467 17592186045585 true] [17592186396183 1077 "selection" 13194139533467 17592186045585 true] [17592186396183 1079 #edb/ref 17592186396185 13194139533467 17592186045585 true] [17592186396183 1080 #uuid "71152846-626d-5dbd-a0ab-1425eb8ae515" 13194139533467 17592186045585 true] [17592186396184 1081 "I only" 13194139533467 17592186045585 true] [17592186396184 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533467 17592186045585 true] [17592186396184 1084 #uuid "9fe865ac-e938-502a-af64-2906292df08f" 13194139533467 17592186045585 true] [17592186396185 1081 "III only" 13194139533467 